{"p4": {"friction": "Remark 4.5's \"△ is isospectral to the Dolbeault-Laplacian\" has no home in the rubric: isospectrality is not one of the equivalent-to senses {iff, isomorphic, equal-value, equivalent-category}, and has-property forbids an object as the predicate.", "doubt": "Claim 6: whether D_(k,γ) is introduced in Remark 1.2 depends on earlier §1 text that is not in the input. Claim 11: the subject is Remark 5.4, while the actual definer is [10]. Claim 13: the object paraphrases (82) instead of stating it in full.", "missing_context": "The body text of §1 before Remark 1.2 (where the perturbation is introduced), and the text around Eq. (108) that Remark 4.7 refers to.", "proposed_change": "Add to equivalent-to §4.6 (Boundary): 'Isospectrality, or any equivalence weaker than identity, isomorphism, equality or logical equivalence, is not equivalent-to; grade wrong-relation.'", "process_observation": "Claims 10 and 12 are near-duplicates (same subject and statement; only the locator detail differs), so the extractor's output needs deduplication. The grader input has duplicate equation labels: Eq. (1) appears twice, and Eq. (3) and Eq. (4) are reused for different formulas."}}
